+Ledgered deltas (the only ones; every other byte matches upstream):
+  D4  ``import pydeck as pdk`` / ``from pydeck.types import String`` are
+      NOT module-top (upstream lines 13/19).  They execute at the top of
+      ``Logger.flow_map_template_1`` (the only consumer) with an
+      actionable ImportError when absent — the reviewed MADINA_ZONAL
+      convention (zonal/utils.py create_deckGL_map).  With pydeck
+      installed the bound objects are identical (sys.modules), so
+      behavior is unchanged; in a pydeck-less environment the module
+      imports and ``Logger``/``betweenness_flow_simulation`` /
+      ``KNN_accessibility`` run, and only map rendering raises.
+
+Pinned workflow-level facts (upstream behavior, carried not fixed —
+parity profiles must reproduce them bitwise; see
+tests/madina_api/workflows and the task evidence):
+  - ``betweenness_flow_simulation`` always calls ``betweenness`` with
+    ``keep_diagnostics=True`` and ``num_cores=min(origin rows,
+    num_cores)``.  With the default ``Closest_destination=True`` the
+    exposure engine's per-origin stats block raises UnboundLocalError
+    (betweenness.py:858-859 read ``eligible_destinations_shortest_
+    distance``, which is assigned ONLY in the Huff branch at :612; the
+    closest-destination branch :582-586 sets
+    ``destination_probabilities=[1]`` without it) AFTER reach/gravity
+    are written; the per-origin handler swallows it, so stats columns
+    (closest_destination_distance, furthest_destination_distance,
+    mean_path_length, probable_travel_distance, eligible_destinations,
+    path_count, ...) stay missing for EVERY origin while edge
+    betweenness still accumulates and the workflow reports success.
+    Empirically the edge record is byte-identical across
+    num_cores in {1, 3} and Turn_Penalty in {0, 30} on the suite
+    fixture (evidence probes 1-2).
+  - ``KNN_accessibility`` rejects ``city_name=None`` even when
+    ``data_folder``/``output_folder`` are explicit (its guard checks
+    only city_name — distinct, shorter ValueError than the flow
+    workflow's).  Its default pairings file is "pairing.csv" (flow's
+    is "pairings.csv"), and it passes
+    ``redundant_edge_treatment='discard'`` explicitly.
+  - ``KNN_accessibility`` CRASHES on a per-row Network_File change:
+    the reload branch calls ``load_layer('streets', ...)`` on a Zonal
+    that already holds that label ->
+    ``KeyError: 'Layer with label streets is already in Zonal
+    object'`` before any row-2 work (row 1's per-pairing
+    origin_record.csv survives; every final output is unreachable).
+    Pinned, not fixed — parity profiles must reproduce it.
+  - A pairing row with no reachable destination (radius below every
+    network path) crashes the KNN workflow with ``KeyError: 'reach'``
+    before ANY output file is written, and an empty pairings table
+    fails at read time with the pandas EmptyDataError.
+  - ``accessibility``'s "equal weight of 1 for all destinations"
+    docstring default does NOT match the observed workflow behavior:
+    with ``Destination_Weight="Count"`` insert_node receives
+    ``weight_attribute=None`` and every destination NODE weight is 1.0
+    (so the hardcoded gravity ``alpha=1`` is bit-inert through that
+    profile), while a real weight attribute engages alpha; the alpha
+    swap is therefore profile-dependent (tests/madina_api/workflows).
+  - The KNN workflow forwards the raw pairing-table cell to
+    ``accessibility(knn_weights=...)``: a bracketed string like
+    "[0.5,0.5]" parses (tools.py str-branch); an empty cell arrives as
+    NaN and raises the verbatim
+    "knn_weight should be a list of numerical values like
+    [0.5, 0.25, 0.25]".
+  - ``Logger.flow_map_template_1`` output HTML is NOT deterministic
+    across runs (same inputs -> different bytes, inside pydeck), so
+    tests pin map presence/size, never content hashes.
+  - ``load_layer`` resets the layer index (zonal.py:89-90), so workflow
+    origin records carry positional ids 0..n-1 regardless of input.
+  - IMPORTING this module writes ``os.environ['USE_PYGEOS'] = '0'``
+    (upstream line 6, carried verbatim): a library-level environment
+    write upstream makes on import.  In-process importers that must
+    keep the process environment pristine (test drivers, embedding
+    applications) should snapshot/restore around the import; parity
+    profiles are unaffected because both arms execute the same write.
+
+Migration examples (upstream Madina -> this facade; the supported
